deploy_amd_dra_driver (lib/Rex/Rancher/K8s.pm ~1473, `docker.io/busybox:1.36`) and deploy_amd_metrics_exporter (~1638, `busybox:1.36`) write upstream's init container image verbatim. It is a mutable tag, not a digest, and the caller has no option to set it, so it is the one image of the AMD stack a consumer cannot pin (OCP pins every other image via OCP::Versions; air-gapped/mirrored clusters may also want their own reference).

Done when: both functions take an optional init image (e.g. `init_image => ...`), default unchanged (busybox:1.36 as upstream), POD names it; or the default is pinned to a digest with a note where it comes from. Either is fine — the point is that the consumer can set it.

